31 reflow-only files, 48 changed lines of pure formatter churn (out of +929/-1665 total). tui_key_hints.dart line 29-30 is a valid anchor.

Now let me also double-check finding A's technical accuracy once more by re-reading the current scheduled_receipts.dart `_drain` + `append` once more in full, so the claim is precise:

Current code (HEAD):
```dart
Future<void> append(String event, Map<String, Object?> fields) {
 final line = jsonEncode({...});
 final next = _tail.then((_) => _write(line));
 _tail = next;
 return next;
}

Future<void> _write(String line) async {
 _pending.add(line);
 await _drain();
}

Future<void> _drain() async {
 while (_pending.isNotEmpty) {
   ... appendFile(path, '${_pending.first}\n') ...
   if (failure != null) {
     if (!_defered) { _defered = true; onError?.call('receipt write deferred (N pending, flushed on recover): ...'); }
     return;
   }
   _pending.removeAt(0);
 }
 _defered = false;
}
``

So flush happens ONLY inside `_drain`, which runs ONLY from `_write`, which runs ONLY from `append`. Confirmed: no idle retry. In a quiet queue (no new scheduled-message lifecycle events), a deferred backlog never flushes, no matter how long the table stays healthy. At process exit (VM death, or the CLI's teardown — no dispose anymore), `_pending` is lost.

Consumer impact: `deliveredIds()` (disk-only) → the obligations reconcile (`agent_cli_persist.dart:_reconcileObligationsLedger`) won't see deferred `delivered` receipts as fired → pending-wait auto-close (issue #2384 AC1) degrades to age-out. On main, pending receipts counted.

Also the old main code documented recovery with a line ('receipt write recovered: N flushed') — gone. And the class doc still claims "a lost receipt must be impossible (a lost receipt = a fired timer that cannot be proven fired)" — under quiet-queue+exit the pending receipt IS lost. The PR description §3 says "A lost receipt is impossible" — overclaim; and its dispose note ("dispose() still drops pending lines") references an API that no longer exists (stale description).

This is one coherent ⚠️ IMPORTANT finding: "the absorbed #2435 design had two pressure-window compensations (idle retry Timer ≤5min; pending-counting in deliveredIds) that this rewrite drops without replacement — a deferred backlog now flushes only on the next append, so in a quiet queue it can sit indefinitely and is lost at process exit; deferred 'delivered' receipts also stop closing obligations-ledger pending-waits (falls back to age-out)."

Proposed fix: keep an idle probe (timer OR a scheduler-tick hook that calls a probe-drain even without events), and/or count pending lines in deliveredIds.

Is it ⚠️ or 🚨? Not data loss in the "user data" sense — receipts are provenance evidence; the failure needs the rare pressure window + quiet queue + exit. The class is best-effort by documented contract (though the doc claims impossibility). ⚠️ IMPORTANT is right.

Finding B: ⚠️ IMPORTANT — 31 reflow-only files / 48 lines of formatter-version churn unrelated to the ticket (tui_key_hints.dart +141/-118 being the largest). Asks: revert the reflow-only files (format with the SDK main uses / only touched files); keep the diff reviewable. Cost stateable: review noise (real changes buried — e.g. the one-line `jobStarted` fix hides inside this), blame pollution, and conflict surface for parallel branches (this PR already absorbed one rebase against #2435).

Hmm — one consideration: is the churn actually caused by a formatter VERSION difference, or did main simply drift? Main's files are formatted with trailing commas in some places (`_pending.take(count).join(),`)... The reflow style (e.g., `'left' || 'h' || 'right' || 'l' =>` split across lines; `width +=\n 2 +\n rows...`) is the Dart 3.7+/3.9 formatter's tall style with the "leading comma-independent" behavior... Actually main's files were formatted by some SDK; the PR's local SDK (3.14/3.50 flutter stable) formats differently. Either way the effect is the same: reformating 31 untouched files. I'll phrase it as "formatter-version drift" without asserting which version.

Finding C: 💡 SUGESTION — `fdLimits()` relaxed the platform gate from (macOS||Linux) to !Windows; on any other POSIX-flavored host an incorrect RLIMIT_* resource number could be read/set (e.g. a BSD where 7 ≠ RLIMIT_NOFILE). Restore the `Platform.isMacOS || Platform.isLinux` gate (one line, restores the old guarantee). 💡 (no officially-supported host is affected).

Digest items (ranked):
1. `lib/src/messaging/scheduled_receipts.dart:_drain` — the recovery notice ('receipt write recovered: N flushed') from the previous impl is gone; recovery is silent. (observability)
2. `lib/src/messaging/scheduled_receipts.dart:_drain` — recovery flushes line-by-line (N appendFile calls), not "the whole backlog ... in ONE append" as the class doc/PR text says; ordering holds, wording doesn't.
3. `lib/src/env/fd_limit_io.dart:raiseFdLimitOnce` — `_raisedOnce` is set BEFORE the attempt, so a refused setrlimit is never retried (intended, matches old refusal semantics, but now implicit); a comment would help.
4. `bin/fah.dart:100-101` — `fdLimits()` is called twice (once for the "before" reading, once inside raiseFdLimitOnce); harmless, could return the before/after pair from one call.
5. PR description staleness: the "dispose() still drops pending lines" note describes an API this PR removed; and "flushes the whole backlog ... on the first successful write" overstates the one-append behavior.

Wait — item 5 is description-vs-diff staleness; that can ride in the general comment.

Also should I double-check `_execRetryNotice`'s `[bash attempt $attempt hit fd pressure` — for attempt=1 → "[bash attempt 1 hit fd pressure (too many open files) — retrying once]". Good.

One more check — the `LocalShell._start` message: 'fd pressure: cannot spawn "$executable" ($error)' — for the classifier `text.contains('fd pressure')`: `$error` interpolated ProcessException — fine.

And the timeout/fd retry interplay in `_execRetryNotice`: if attempt 1 is fdExhausted → retry; attempt 2 also fdExhausted → null → `_bashFailureError` → default arm → StateError('...ExecutionError(fdExhausted): fd pressure: cannot spawn...') — hmm, `$error` renders ExecutionError.toString(). Does toString include 'ExecutionError(fdExhausted): '? The test fake message includes that prefix and the agent_loop test expects contains('fd pressure') and NOT contains('uncaught'). The real path: `_bashFailureError` default arm → `'${_retryNoticePrefix(notices)}$error'` → ExecutionError.toString() — let me confirm it includes the message. Check toString impl.

